13. The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press **Add another payment (paid in parts)** and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.
14. Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.
15. The rental agreement: Send it to sign online, or Already signed on paper (a task asks for the scan). The calendar: untick Blocks the car''s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.
16. Tick **Do not email the renter** if they should not get the confirmation. Press **Add the rental**.

> Tip: The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal, or on paper and you record it. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, **Verified in person** records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.

## Retire or delete a car

**Cars** > **Retire or delete**, or the car''s own page.

1. **Retire this car** takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. **Restore** brings it back.
2. **Delete this car** removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.
3. Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.
4. On the same page, **Delete all sample cars** deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.

## Sample cars on the site

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, or **Settings** > **Site**. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.

1. **Hide sample cars** asks first ("Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?"); press **Hide them** to take every sample car off the site at once, or **Keep them**. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.
2. **Show sample cars** puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.
3. On the site each one is marked "Example car". They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.
4. A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.

> Tip: Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.

## Why a car is not on the site yet

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the card Not on the site yet.

1. Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.
2. The same car is a line on To do with **Set rates and publish**. The car comes off both once it is on the site.
3. A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.

## Placeholder bookings

A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.

1. On **Add a rental**, press **Placeholder** (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.
2. Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.
3. A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, **More actions** > **Mark as a placeholder**. Not once money was taken or the car went out. **Make it a real booking** undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.
4. On the booking, **Competing for these dates** (and **Also on this car for these dates** once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.

## Tolls when two rentals overlap

Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">A car comes from one of three places: a program owner, CarmaCars itself, or a partner rental company. You add cars and rentals by hand, retire cars, and delete cars that were added by mistake.</p><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-add-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>. Start with the VIN: everything else about the car comes from it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type or paste the VIN. At the 17th character the car is looked up: one line shows the year, make, model, trim, body, seats, doors, fuel, drive, gearbox and engine. Press Edit only if something is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the VIN fits several trims, the form asks which trim it is: press the one on the car&#39;s papers or badge, or <b class="gd-ui">Not sure</b> (Admin &gt; Today asks again).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">No VIN at hand? Press <b class="gd-ui">No VIN at hand? Add the car by its plate</b> and choose the year, make and model from the lists. The VIN can be added later; the details fill in then.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Tap the colour (it is not in the VIN). Leave it empty and it is read from the cover photo once the car has one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Check the class. It is set from the make, model, body and age (a 2016 Porsche Macan is Premium, an SUV is SUV) and the line under it says why. Change it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Choose who supplies it: <b class="gd-ui">A program owner&#39;s car</b> (choose the owner; the car starts its onboarding), <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars-owned (company fleet)</b> (no owner; all of its revenue is CarmaCars&#39;) or <b class="gd-ui">A partner rental company&#39;s car</b> (choose the partner; leave the commission empty to use the partner&#39;s).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The daily rate is filled in from similar cars, else the class. Keep it, change it, or empty it and set the rates later on the car&#39;s Rates tab. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the car</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The title, description and features are written by themselves right after the car is added, from the VIN details. Change any of them on the car&#39;s listing; a field you change is kept.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every car gets a fleet number and its standard settings the moment it is added: a complete rate card (the daily rate you typed or the suggested one, weekend, weekly and monthly from it, the kilometres a day, the extra kilometre rate, the deposit and the delivery and pickup fee of its class) and drivers 18 to 20 allowed. Each value set this way says (Set automatically) on the car&#39;s Overview and Rates tab until you change it. The defaults come from Settings: Program and Fee defaults.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A VIN that does not add up (one character misread) shows a warning; you can still save it. A VIN the decoder cannot read asks only the year, make and model and never stops you: the details fill in when it is read later. The duplicate check runs as for every car: a VIN only once, a plate on one active car, and a likely twin waits for you in Similar cars before it is published.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The gearbox comes from the government&#39;s fuel economy data for the model when it has one gearbox for it, or from the VIN when the VIN states it. Seats come from the VIN, or the usual number for the body (4 for a coupe or convertible, 5 for a sedan, SUV or hatchback). When either is not certain, Admin &gt; Today shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirm gearbox and seats</b>: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows <b class="gd-ui">Pick the trim</b> there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.</p><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b> shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-partners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a partner</b>: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Banking (Admins only): <b class="gd-ui">Save the payout account</b> for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b> once checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Portal: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to the owner portal</b> gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Signed on paper? Press <b class="gd-ui">Print the partner agreement</b>, then record the signed scan under Record a paper signature.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-fleet-on-its-own-rates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner fleet on its own rates</h2><p class="gd-p">Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> &gt; the partner. <b class="gd-ui">Pricing</b> shows how it is paid: the renter pays the partner&#39;s sheet rate plus the markup (10% unless you set another), rounded to the nearest dollar; CarmaCars keeps the markup plus its cut (20% of the sheet rate); the partner is owed the rest of its sheet rate. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit pricing</b> to change the markup, the cut or the basis for every car at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> lists each car with its sheet rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and the renter&#39;s rates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own markup or cut, mark it <b class="gd-ui">Insurance included</b> or <b class="gd-ui">No credit card needed</b>, or confirm its model year. The renter&#39;s rates change at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and &quot;Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review&quot;. A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says &quot;Year confirmed when you book&quot;; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car&#39;s page before its first handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), <b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The partner&#39;s monthly statement shows each rental at the sheet rate, the cut and the payout; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner&#39;s share in proportion; a discount CarmaCars gives comes out of the markup.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-s-crm-01-motors-gohighlevel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner&#39;s CRM (01 Motors&#39; GoHighLevel)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> tile, then the partner (or <b class="gd-ui">CRM link</b> on the partner&#39;s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box <b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors gives us</b> on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press <b class="gd-ui">Connect</b>. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. <b class="gd-ui">Test connection</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Run sync now</b> do it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors sees</b>: CarmaCars&#39; own cars and program owners&#39; cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a &quot;CarmaCars Vehicles&quot; object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner&#39;s. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change what we share</b> to leave out program owners&#39; cars, rates, availability or photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Partner price</b>: the site&#39;s rates, or the site&#39;s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Their cars coming in</b>: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows <b class="gd-ui">Add as their car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Leads both ways</b> (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Feed, widget and booking links</b>: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/&lt;car&gt; that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin &gt; Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-add-a-rental-by-hand" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental by hand</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> at the top of Bookings (or on To do). For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Standing with the renter at pickup? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: type the renter&#39;s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner using own car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter&#39;s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner&#39;s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b> once the insurer confirms it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer&#39;s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press <b class="gd-ui">Add another payment (paid in parts)</b> and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">15</span><div class="gd-t">The rental agreement: Send it to sign online, or Already signed on paper (a task asks for the scan). The calendar: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">16</span><div class="gd-t">Tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b> if they should not get the confirmation. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal, or on paper and you record it. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Verified in person</b> records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-retire-or-delete-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Retire or delete a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Retire or delete</b>, or the car&#39;s own page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Retire this car</b> takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> brings it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete this car</b> removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the same page, <b class="gd-ui">Delete all sample cars</b> deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-sample-cars-on-the-site" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample cars on the site</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site</b>. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide sample cars</b> asks first (&quot;Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?&quot;); press <b class="gd-ui">Hide them</b> to take every sample car off the site at once, or <b class="gd-ui">Keep them</b>. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show sample cars</b> puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the site each one is marked &quot;Example car&quot;. They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-why-a-car-is-not-on-the-site-yet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Why a car is not on the site yet</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the card Not on the site yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The same car is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The car comes off both once it is on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-placeholder-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Placeholder bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b> (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a placeholder</b>. Not once money was taken or the car went out. <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking</b> undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Competing for these dates</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Also on this car for these dates</b> once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-tolls-when-two-rentals-overlap" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tolls when two rentals overlap</h2><p class="gd-p">Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'chauffeur-service', 'chapter', 'insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing', 'Visitors book a driver and a luxury car or van by the hour on carmacars.ca/chauffeur. The vehicles come from a partner''s chauffeur price guide, each with a rate for 2 hours and a rate for 3 hours or more.

:::flow
Request | The visitor sends the date, hours and addresses
Quote | You check with the partner and send the quote
Confirm | The client agrees and pays
Done | Mark it completed after the trip
:::

## The requests

**Bookings** > **Chauffeur**. Each request has its number (CH-1001 and up), the vehicle, the date and start time, the hours, the pickup and drop-off addresses, the passengers, the occasion and the notes.

1. The **Quote** column is the price for the client: the hours at the 2-hour rate (exactly 2 hours) or the 3+ hour rate (3 hours or more), before HST, then HST and the total. The line under it is the quote line to send.
2. **Partner, CarmaCars** shows the partner''s sheet amount, what the partner is owed (the sheet amount less the cut) and what CarmaCars keeps (the markup plus the cut).
3. Check the vehicle and the driver with the partner for that time. To change the vehicle or the hours, press **Change**: the quote is worked out again.
4. Send the quote line by email or phone, then press **Quoted** and say how you sent it. The task in the queue is done.
5. When the client agrees, take the payment (a payment link, or at pickup), press **Confirm** and note how it is paid.
6. After the trip press **Completed**. **Decline** or **Cancel** closes a request with the reason.

> Tip: To do has a line **Chauffeur requests to quote** while any request is new, and the card Chauffeur today lists the confirmed trips of the day.

## The vehicles and their rates

**People** > **Partners** > the partner, card Chauffeur vehicles.

1. Each vehicle shows the partner''s rates an hour and the client''s (the markup added, rounded to the nearest dollar).
2. Press **Edit** to change a rate, give it its own markup or cut, change the passengers, or take it off the site.
3. A vehicle the partner also rents (chauffeur / rental) links to its car pages on the public page.

> Good to know: Booking requests for cars, offers and payments do not cover chauffeur trips: a chauffeur request is a quote that you send and confirm here.
', 'Chauffeur service', 'Chauffeur requests: quote, confirm and close them; the vehicles and their hourly rates.',
