om Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-out: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. The search above it finds any booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'shared-tools', 'chapter', 'car-maintenance', 'Every function has the calendar and Find a renter. Use them to answer questions fast.

## The calendar

1. Every car, its bookings, requests and blocks. The red line is now.
2. Use the arrows, Today and the range to move around, or search by plate, booking or name.
3. Fleet and customer service can remove a cleaning block from its side panel (**Remove the block**) when a car is ready sooner.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-09-calendar-desktop-541a6da5.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 800; address: carmacars.ca/va/calendar; pins: 1 60.2 33.8, 2 28.5 17.5")

## Find a car

**Bookings** > **Find a car** (Finance and Fleet: **Rentals** > **Find a car**). A renter quotes the car code on the car''s page (like CC-7F3A).

1. Type the car code, a plate, a VIN or the name. Each car shows its code, plate, status and its page on the site.
2. In Add a rental, type the car code or plate in the box above Car to choose it.

## Find a renter

1. Search by name, email, phone or booking number.
2. Opening a renter''s private details asks for a reason (**Open with a reason**). It is kept in the access log.

![](/guides/img/va-cs-07-renters-desktop-99cfd0ef.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 240; address: carmacars.ca/va/renters; pins: 1 68.3 34.6")

## Email the renter

Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance can all write to the renter from a booking: press **Email the renter**, or open the **Messages** tab.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from.
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars and the renter can answer in their account; the answer opens a task for customer service.
3. On a booking an insurer pays you can choose Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance) as the sender, and **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster on the booking.

The tab lists the messages both ways and every email of the booking with its state. Each email counts against the daily email limit, shown under the form.

### Find a booking
**Rentals** > **Find a booking**: type at least 3 characters of the booking number (CC-1042, 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number, a plate or a car code, then press Enter. Every search is logged, as Find a renter.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer for new requests, replies to answer and urgent problems, even with the portal closed.

1. Open **Profile** (top of the menu). Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications. The first page of the portal also offers it once.
2. Under **What to alert me about**: new requests, booking changes and messages are on for staff; payments are off until you tick them.
3. **Send a test alert** checks the device. **Remove** takes an old phone off.

On an iPhone, add CarmaCars to the Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**). Use your phone''s own Focus or Do Not Disturb for quiet hours.', 'Shared tools', 'The calendar and Find a renter.',
